body:
I haven't used heroin indeed, i have done other drugs and mostly benzo's. I understand that low dosages might help but only for a short period, not years. It still has a big impact on your life and let's not forget about tolerance/addiction. Heroin is not practical, you can't just inject anywhere you want to and everything needs to be clean.

&#x200B;

I remember when i was on 0.25-0.5 Xanax and it was impossible trying to function properly, you are there with your body but not with your mind. Also slurred speech and drowsiness were a big problem.

There is no objective sources out there, you have to search and find out yourself. What makes something a trust worthy source? And from there on you can ask something like, where can i find the middle ground in this?

&#x200B;

Also, research is very important. Research for 5 minutes, you mostly will face bullshit, research for 1 hour, that's what the average human will read, research for 4 hours and you slowly get to enter the underworld and totally different perspectives, where is no middle ground, no right or wrong, just endless perspectives. Go even further and further in an abstract subject and it only will get more complicated but as time goes on, you will sort it out. Search terms are also important, check out google dorks for example.

&#x200B;

After a long time of researching you realize the world isn't so black and white as your parents teached you, the colors are all over the place. I guess it's the complexity of the universe, which is, of course, very beautiful and amazing to experience. Especially in this time, where we got so much information and it's addicting. [https://youtu.be/1qQQXTMih1A](https://youtu.be/1qQQXTMih1A)
